    "body": "### Problem\n\nHi,\n\nWith low-contrast color schemes, it is difficult to distinguish between the content of the documentation popup and the content of the buffer. There is no spacing between them, and setting the background to a different color does not help much either.\n\nI think it would be great to add a border to the documentation popup.\n\nPossible solutions would be:\n\n1) Use the global winborder property for this.\n2) Introduce a dedicated popup-border property.\n3) Add spacer rows/columns around the documentation content (which I think would be a bad solution).\n\nWhat do you think? Which solution should we choose? Option 1 would break users' current expectations.\nLet me know if you’re happy with the approach below. If so, I’ll create a PR.\n\n\n\n\n\nI made a small adjustment to `share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/completion.lua` that works for my needs.\n```lua\n--- share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/completion.lua\n--- ...\nlocal function update_popup_window(winid, bufnr, kind)\n    if winid and api.nvim_win_is_valid(winid) and bufnr and api.nvim_buf_is_valid(bufnr) then\n        if kind == lsp.protocol.MarkupKind.Markdown then\n            vim.wo[winid].conceallevel = 2\n            vim.treesitter.start(bufnr, kind)\n        end\n        local winborder = vim.o.winborder\n        if winborder ~= \"\" and winborder ~= \"none\" then\n            local config = api.nvim_win_get_config(winid)\n            config.border = vim.o.winborder\n            api.nvim_win_set_config(winid, config)\n        end\n        local all = api.nvim_win_text_height(winid).all\n        api.nvim_win_resize(winid, -1, all)\n    end\nend\n--- ....\n```\n\n<img width=\"2547\" height=\"1563\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/23a11a8a-c3c0-4183-920d-e58636cd0a7e\" />\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n-",
